# Copy to .env for local development against a real backend. .env is gitignored;
# on a host (Vercel, Firebase) set these as environment variables instead.
#
# Leave everything unset and the app uses local disk + memory — `npm start`
# needs no cloud account at all.

# ---- Supabase (recommended when hosted) ----
# SUPABASE_URL: Project Settings -> API -> Project URL
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: the "secret" key (sb_secret_...) on newer projects,
#   or the legacy "service_role" JWT. It bypasses row-level security, so it is
#   server-side only and must never reach the browser or the repo.
# The "publishable"/anon key is NOT used by this app.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_BUCKET=selfies
# SUPABASE_TABLE=submissions

# ---- Automatic content moderation (OpenAI) ----
# Screens the name, the message and the photo before anything is stored.
# Flagged uploads are refused outright; a missing key simply turns the filter
# off, which is why `npm start` still works with no OpenAI account.
# Get one at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys — server-side only.
OPENAI_MODERATION_APIKEY=
# OPENAI_MODERATION_MODEL=omni-moderation-latest   (must be a vision-capable
#   moderation model; the older text-moderation-* models cannot see photos)
# MODERATION_TIMEOUT_MS=8000        how long to wait before giving up and
#                                   letting the upload through unchecked
# MODERATION_THRESHOLD=0.5          optional 0-1 tightening. Unset means the
#                                   API's own verdict decides. Lower is
#                                   stricter, and more false rejections.
# MODERATION_MAX_IMAGE_BYTES=6291456  photos larger than this skip the image
#                                   check rather than stall the upload

# ---- Force a specific driver (optional) ----
# STORAGE_DRIVER=local|supabase|firebase|vercel

# ---- QR target for a LAN demo (optional) ----
# PUBLIC_URL=http://192.168.1.20:3000
